-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Note for the authors (delete this section when you replace this file with the licence text)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. The manuscript describes TODSphere as "open-source". The terms shipped with the paper build
   (TODSphere-Build_v2/LICENSE.txt: free for education and research, no commercial distribution) are
   NOT an open-source licence under the OSI definition. Please pick an OSI-approved licence, or change
   the wording in the manuscript.
2. Recommended options:
   - MIT: permissive and short, compatible with every vendored library. Most common for research tools.
   - Apache-2.0: permissive, with an explicit patent grant.
   - GPL-3.0-or-later or AGPL-3.0-or-later: copyleft, so derivative tools must stay open. AGPL also
     covers use as a hosted web service.
   Check any policy of your institution (Shiv Nadar Institution of Eminence) on software ownership
   before you choose.
3. How to apply the licence:
   - Replace this whole file with the unmodified licence text (for example from
     https://choosealicense.com). Keep the copyright line.
   - Set "license" in package.json to the SPDX identifier (e.g. "MIT").
   - Set "license" in CITATION.cff and .zenodo.json to the same identifier.
   Zenodo requires a licence for the software record.
4. The manuscript data in data/paper/ derive from ODbL and CC BY 4.0 sources. If you license the data
   separately (e.g. ODbL for the OSM-derived tables), say so in README.md.
